{"id":1106,"date":"2020-11-20T13:12:46","date_gmt":"2020-11-20T21:12:46","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1106"},"modified":"2024-09-01T20:23:08","modified_gmt":"2024-09-02T03:23:08","slug":"codrone-arduino-flags","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-flags\/","title":{"rendered":"Flags"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1cde7\" name=\"6a2215cd1cde7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are event flags?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Flags are a little like switches that trigger different events in your program depending on whether they&#8217;re on (a value of 1) or off (a value of 0). One way to think of it is like the flags on mailboxes. If the flag is up, that means the mail carrier has something to pick up. If the flag is down, that means there is nothing for the mail carrier to pick up.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1107&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]In programming, flags are usually used with if, else if, and else statements, with the flag as the conditional and the event as the action that will be performed if the statement is true.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if (flag == 0){\r\n    event 1;\r\n}\r\n\r\nelse if (flag == 1){\r\n    event 2;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>For this program, if the flag has a value of 0, event 1 will happen. If the flag has a value of 1, event 2 will happen.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1cf47\" name=\"6a2215cd1cf47\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flag setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Flags are variables that perform a specific function, and just like any other variable, you need to initialize it in your program before you can use it. After including your CoDrone library, declare these variables in Arduino:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include&lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint move_flag;\r\nint fly_flag;\r\nint counter;<\/pre>\n<p>Next, in void setup, you&#8217;re going to connect your drone, change the drone mode to flight, and set all of the variables&#8217; values to 0.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void setup() {\r\n CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n CoDrone.pair();\r\n CoDrone.DroneModeChange(Flight); \r\n \r\n move_flag = 0;\r\n fly_flag = 0;\r\n counter = 0;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>Wondering what counter even means and why we would include it? We&#8217;ll explain!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1cfb0\" name=\"6a2215cd1cfb0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are counters?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Really quick detour: counters are a way to break your code up into steps and keep track of which step you&#8217;re on. Just like flags, you need to set them up as a variable at the beginning of your program (which you did during the last step), and you can use them with if, else if, and else statements.<\/p>\n<p>This is what a counter program usually looks like:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int counter = 0; \r\nvoid setup(){\r\n}\r\nvoid loop(){\r\n  if (counter == 0){\r\n    \/\/ code for step 1\r\n    counter = 1;\r\n }\r\n  else if (counter == 1){\r\n    \/\/ code for step 2\r\n    counter = 2;\r\n  }\r\n  else if (counter == 2){\r\n    \/\/ code for step 3\r\n    counter = 3;\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1d00b\" name=\"6a2215cd1d00b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wait for it...<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You only need to use one sensor in your program, and that&#8217;s going to be sensor 11! In void loop, initialize sensor 11 as an input, and then write your program so that if sensor 11 is triggered (which means you&#8217;re covering it), your CoDrone will stop.<\/p>\n<p>You&#8217;re probably thinking, &#8220;But Robolink! It hasn&#8217;t even taken off yet! Why would it stop?!&#8221; This is mostly so your CoDrone doesn&#8217;t immediately hit the ceiling once you cover sensor 11. For your next line, you&#8217;re going to include a delay of 1 second and then have the counter add 1 to itself after that second is up. We promise something will happen in the next step.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n\r\n if( bt1 ){\r\n   CoDrone.FlightEvent(Stop); \r\n   CoDrone.move(1);\r\n   counter++;\r\n }<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1d078\" name=\"6a2215cd1d078\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add your counters<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Remember that we said that a value of 1 would be added to the counter every second that sensor 11 was triggered? This is where your flags will start to come together with the counter!<\/p>\n<p>First, create an if statement so that if the counter is 3, <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">fly_flag<\/code> is 1. Don&#8217;t worry, we&#8217;ll talk about what <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">fly_flag<\/code> is in the next step, but you can guess in the meantime!<\/p>\n<p>Next, create an if statement so that if the counter is 6, <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">move_flag<\/code> is 1. Again, next step, you can guess.<\/p>\n<p>Finally, create another if statement so that if the counter is 9, your CoDrone lands. Wait! It didn&#8217;t even take off yet! What happened?! Again, we&#8217;ll explain in the next step.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if(counter == 3){\r\n   fly_flag = 1;\r\n }\r\n if(counter == 6){\r\n   move_flag = 1;\r\n }\r\n if(counter == 9){\r\n   CoDrone.setPitch(0);\r\n   CoDrone.move(0.5);\r\n   CoDrone.land();\r\n }<\/pre>\n<div class=\"CodeMirror notranslate cm-s-default\">\n<div><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1d0d8\" name=\"6a2215cd1d0d8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flag events<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you guessed that <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">fly_flag<\/code> means that the CoDrone is going to fly, you were right! Write an if statement so that if the value of <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">fly_flag<\/code> is 1, the CoDrone will take off and play a sound on the buzzer. Make sure you include a line that changes the value of <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">fly_flag<\/code> back to 0 so that the CoDrone only takes off once and doesn&#8217;t hit the ceiling.<\/p>\n<p>If you guessed that <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">move_flag<\/code> means that the CoDrone is going to move, you were right! Write an if statement so that if the value of <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">move_flag<\/code> is 1, the CoDrone will pitch forward at 50 and play a sound on the buzzer.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if(fly_flag == 1){\r\n   CoDrone.takeoff();\r\n   fly_flag = 0;\r\n   CoDrone.Buzz(400,4);\r\n }\r\n\r\n if(move_flag == 1){\r\n   CoDrone.setPitch(50);\r\n   CoDrone.Buzz(400,4);\r\n }<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1d15b\" name=\"6a2215cd1d15b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This is what your final code should look like:<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include&lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint move_flag;\r\nint fly_flag;\r\nint counter;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n CoDrone.pair();\r\n CoDrone.DroneModeChange(Flight); \r\n \r\n move_flag = 0;\r\n fly_flag = 0;\r\n counter = 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n \r\n if( bt1 ){\r\n   CoDrone.emergencyStop(); \/\/kill switch\r\n   CoDrone.move(1);\r\n   counter++;\r\n }\r\n\r\n if(counter == 3){\r\n   fly_flag = 1;\r\n }\r\n\r\n if(counter == 6){\r\n   move_flag = 1;\r\n }\r\n\r\n if(counter == 9){\r\n   CoDrone.setPitch(0);\r\n   CoDrone.move(0.5);\r\n   CoDrone.land();\r\n }\r\n\r\n \/\/flag trigger takeoff the drone\r\n if(fly_flag == 1){\r\n   CoDrone.takeoff();\r\n   fly_flag = 0;\r\n   CoDrone.Buzz(400,4);\r\n }\r\n\r\n\/\/ move trigger make drone go forward\r\n if(move_flag == 1){\r\n   CoDrone.setPitch(50);\r\n   CoDrone.move();\r\n   CoDrone.Buzz(400,4);\r\n }\r\n \r\n}<\/pre>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>This is the pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Include the CoDrone library.<\/li>\n<li>Initialize move_flag, fly_flag, and counter variables.<\/li>\n<li>Start communication at a baud rate of 115200.<\/li>\n<li>Connect to a nearby drone.<\/li>\n<li>Set the CoDrone&#8217;s mode to flight.<\/li>\n<li>Set all of the variables&#8217; values to 0.<\/li>\n<li>Establish sensor 11 as an input.<\/li>\n<li>If sensor 11 is triggered, add a value of 1 to the counter every second.<\/li>\n<li>If the counter is at 3, take off, play a sound on the buzzer, and set fly_flag to 0.<\/li>\n<li>If the counter is at 6, pitch forward for 50 and play a sound on the buzzer.<\/li>\n<li>If the counter is at 9, stop pitching forward for 0.5 seconds and then land.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215cd1d1c9\" name=\"6a2215cd1d1c9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p><strong>Challenge: Dizzy Drone<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Use what you learned in this lesson to make your drone spin!<\/p>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your drone must take off, spin, and land.<\/li>\n<li>Your program must use flags and counters.<\/li>\n<li>If you need another challenge, have your drone move either pitch or roll after spinning!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__question\">\n<div class=\"styled-checkbox activity2__button-checkbox\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 What are event flags? [vc_column_text]Flags are a little like switches that trigger different events in your program depending on whether they're on (a value of 1) or&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-flags\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1749,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1737,1782,1848,1793,1826,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2195,2163,2164,2165,2196,2194,2122],"class_list":["post-1106","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-advanced","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-counters","lesson-tag-flags","lesson-tag-programming","module-advanced","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1106","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1106\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1108,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1106\/revisions\/1108"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1749"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1106"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1106"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1106"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}